# @@PROJECT_NAME_HEADING@@

This is a project-local, explicitly invoked skill generated by `long-term-project-manager`.

## Load every time

1. Read `framework/version.json` and `views/project-map.json` before proposing or doing project work.
2. Treat `views/project-map.json` as a directly loaded, derived navigation view. Formal accepted records and typed relations in `records/` are authoritative. Never change project state by editing a view.
3. Do not load `records/` wholesale. Read only `records/store.json` entries or `records/materials/` files referenced by the current map nodes or task when the view lacks needed detail.
4. On the first invocation on a machine, locate the explicitly installed `long-term-project-manager` skill and read its confirmed private machine profile if present. Use it only for capability selection; never copy it into this project or an export.

## High-priority framework rules

- Work in one declared role: `maintainer`, `explorer`, or `integrator`. If the requested role is ambiguous and changes write authority, resolve it with the user before changing state.
- Before a substantive task, confirm or reuse a task contract covering result, scope, non-goals, acceptance evidence, allowed side effects, and stop condition.
- Prefer `discover an existing AI/tool capability -> create or adapt the smallest justified tool -> use the tool`. Put reusable new tools in `work/candidate-tools/` and ask about retention at task close.
- Execute confirmed high-priority tasks before low-priority tasks unless the user explicitly selects otherwise.
- Only the maintainer/integrator may change `records/` or archived decisions, and only after itemized proposals are individually accepted. After one accepted batch, increment the formal revision once, regenerate `views/`, and validate.
- The explorer may write pending material under `work/` and change normal project artifacts when authorized by the task contract, but must not change `records/`, `views/`, or archived decisions. Read `framework/conditional/explore.md` and finish with a `.llmpack` handoff.
- The integrator must read `framework/conditional/integrate.md`. Verification and proposal come before commit; imported code is never executed automatically.
- Never add, remove, reprioritize, or close a task without user confirmation. Never silently convert an idea or finding into a task.

## Low-priority modules

- Read `framework/conditional/explore.md` only for exploration or packaging.
- Read `framework/conditional/integrate.md` only for package review and integration.
- Read `framework/conditional/tool-lifecycle.md` when a candidate tool is created or imported.
